# =============================================================================
#  Decay with STATE-DEPENDENT measurement noise    A --k--> (gone)
# =============================================================================
#  A single first-order decay, A(t) = A0 exp(-k t), from A0 = 1000, measured with
#  a COMBINED additive+proportional error: the standard deviation of each point is
#
#        sigma(t) = sd_abs + sd_rel * A(t)
#
#  an additive floor `sd_abs` PLUS a term proportional to the predicted signal
#  `sd_rel * A`. This is the honest heteroscedastic error model an assay with both a
#  constant baseline noise AND a signal-proportional component actually has -- large
#  absolute scatter where the signal is big, a fixed noise floor where it decays away.
#
#  Only k is a model parameter. sd_abs and sd_rel are NUISANCE parameters (named free
#  variables the noise-model line binds its sigma expression to), not part of the
#  model -- the fit estimates all three jointly. Because sigma is a function of the
#  PREDICTED state A, it cannot be supplied as a fixed _SD data column: the fit reads
#  it from the simulation via `sigma = prediction_formula sd_abs + sd_rel*Obs_A`
#  (lesson 48). This is the noise-side peer of a measurement model (ADR-0075).
# =============================================================================

begin model

begin parameters
  k   0.4    # decay rate [1/day]  <- FITTED
  A0  1000   # initial amount [AU] (fixed/known) -- a wide dynamic range so the signal-
             # proportional noise term dominates the early points and the floor the late ones
end parameters

begin molecule types
  A()
end molecule types

begin seed species
  A()  A0
end seed species

begin observables
  Molecules  Obs_A  A()
end observables

begin reaction rules
  A_decay: A() -> 0  k
end reaction rules

end model
